  "notes": "{憤|いきどお}る expresses strong anger with a moral or righteous quality.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive)\n- Pattern: ～に{憤|いきどお}る (to be indignant at ~)\n\nGodan verb ({五段動詞|ごだんどうし}), る-ending.\n- Negative: {憤|いきどお}らない\n- Te-form: {憤|いきどお}って\n- Past: {憤|いきどお}った\n- Noun form: {憤|いきどお}り (indignation)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {不正|ふせい}に{憤|いきどお}る: to be indignant at injustice\n- {憤|いきどお}りを{覚|おぼ}える: to feel indignation\n- {憤|いきどお}りを{抑|おさ}える: to suppress one's indignation\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {憤|いきどお}る: to be indignant (righteous anger, moral outrage)\n- {怒|おこ}る: to get angry (general anger)\n- {腹|はら}が{立|た}つ: to be irritated, annoyed (personal frustration)\n- {激怒|げきど}する: to be enraged (extreme anger, formal)",
